<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Jordan cuts tariff on Australian sugar, rice.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Jordan cuts tariff on Australian sugar, rice.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan would make permanent an interim reduction to five percent from 50 percent in the tariff it applied to Australian sugar and rice, Australian Trade Minister Tim Fischer said in a statement.</p>
<p>This undertaking was given by Jordan's Prime Minister Abdul Karim Al Kabariti at meetings in Jordan, said Fischer, who is on a 10-day trade visit to the Middle East.</p>
<p>The interim tariff cut was due to expire in April.</p>
<p>The Australian sugar industry would also be able to supply an extra 16,000 tonnes of sugar to the U.S. this year as a result of an increase in U.S. raw sugar tariff quotas, he said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-18900</p>
</text>
